<main>
    <section id="overview">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>The environment is facing numerous challenges that threaten the health of our planet. These challenges include climate change, pollution, and the loss of biodiversity. In this article, we explore these issues and the steps we can take to help protect the environment.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="climate-change">
        <h2>Climate Change</h2>
        <article>
            <h3>What is Climate Change?</h3>
            <p>Climate change refers to significant changes in global temperatures and weather patterns over time. The current trend is largely driven by human activities, such as the burning of fossil fuels, deforestation, and industrial activities.</p>
            <figure>
                <img src="climate-change.jpg" alt="Climate Change Effects">
                <figcaption>Figure 1: The impact of climate change on the environment.</figcaption>
            </figure>
        </article>
        <aside>
            <h3>Interesting Facts</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>2020 was one of the hottest years on record.</li>
                <li>Ice caps are melting at an accelerated rate.</li>
            </ul>
        </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="biodiversity">
        <h2>Biodiversity Loss</h2>
        <article>
            <h3>The Importance of Biodiversity</h3>
            <p>Biodiversity refers to the variety of life on Earth, including animals, plants, and microorganisms. Healthy ecosystems rely on biodiversity to function properly. The loss of biodiversity poses a threat to human survival as well.</p>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section id="solutions">
        <h2>What Can We Do to Help?</h2>
        <details>
            <summary>Reduce Waste</summary>
            <p>Reducing waste can help lower pollution and save natural resources. Recycling, reusing, and composting are great ways to minimize waste.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
            <summary>Support Renewable Energy</summary>
            <p>Switching to renewable energy sources like wind, solar, and hydropower can help reduce our reliance on fossil fuels and lower greenhouse gas emissions.</p>
        </details>

